WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:37.690
This is my story
as I remember it


00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:44.941
HOPE


00:01:58.237 --> 00:02:00.321
Thank you.


00:02:03.488 --> 00:02:05.863
-Bye.
-Goodbye.


00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.988
Hi!


00:02:31.407 --> 00:02:34.282
-We're making a gingerbread castle!
-I can tell.


00:02:34.407 --> 00:02:37.324
-Look at this.
-Oops.


00:02:42.532 --> 00:02:45.907
-Hello?
-Hello!


00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.074
Hi.


00:02:48.199 --> 00:02:50.532
Hi, dear.


00:02:50.657 --> 00:02:53.990
-Hi.
-Good to see you.


00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.617
Wow! Look at this!


00:03:08.742 --> 00:03:12.242
Hi!
How's it gone here?


00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:15.659
-Henrik and Ada took care of us.
-What about me?


00:03:15.784 --> 00:03:19.409
Haven't I taken care of you?
And made dinner?


00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:23.452
-Hi.
-Yes, twice in four weeks.


00:03:23.577 --> 00:03:27.785
If you're that ungrateful, I don't mind.
I'm leaving.


00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:32.994
-I'm going out with some friends.
-Okay. Bye. See you.


00:03:34.078 --> 00:03:36.078
Where's Dad?


00:03:36.203 --> 00:03:40.494
-He's working late.
-As usual.


00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:42.619
Bye!


00:03:42.744 --> 00:03:46.078
Will you help decorate the tree tomorrow?


00:03:47.453 --> 00:03:51.329
-When are we going to buy the tree?
-Tomorrow.


00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.204
How are you doing?


00:03:56.329 --> 00:03:58.120
Okay.


00:03:58.245 --> 00:04:00.870
-Okay?
-Yes.


00:04:04.245 --> 00:04:06.913
Her heart is broken.


00:04:07.038 --> 00:04:11.621
-I heard her tell Dad.
-Were you spying again?


00:04:11.746 --> 00:04:14.913
How else am I supposed
to find out anything?


00:04:15.038 --> 00:04:17.164
Hey...


00:04:26.289 --> 00:04:28.706
What's going on here?


00:04:53.791 --> 00:04:55.874
But hey...


00:04:55.999 --> 00:05:01.374
We agreed that you wouldn't work evenings.
I never do when you're away.


00:05:01.499 --> 00:05:04.958
Take it easy. Everything went fine.


00:05:05.083 --> 00:05:07.416
I took care of it my way.


00:05:07.541 --> 00:05:10.876
Using the older kids as babysitters?


00:05:14.835 --> 00:05:17.543
Seen any reviews?


00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:22.543
Yes, there have been a couple.


00:05:22.668 --> 00:05:26.960
-And?
-They were pretty short. But favorable.


00:05:28.751 --> 00:05:31.960
Not like in theatre,
where they're neither?


00:05:41.669 --> 00:05:44.545
Could you turn off the light?


00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:48.378
-You want me to go to the study?
-Not really.


00:05:48.503 --> 00:05:51.628
I can't seem to get rid of this headache.


00:05:51.753 --> 00:05:56.170
It's just as bad in the morning
as when I go to bed at night.


00:05:56.295 --> 00:05:59.170
Right, lousy hotel beds.


00:05:59.295 --> 00:06:01.378
And stress.


00:06:09.879 --> 00:06:14.254
The day before Christmas Eve


00:06:15.004 --> 00:06:18.505
I got these after an optical checkup.


00:06:22.672 --> 00:06:25.839
-Right, reading glasses?
-Yes.


00:06:25.964 --> 00:06:29.090
Custom-made prism lenses.


00:06:29.215 --> 00:06:34.048
-But I still can't read. I just get dizzy.
-I see.


00:06:42.256 --> 00:06:45.548
I want you to take an MRI scan.


00:06:47.548 --> 00:06:51.341
-When?
-Now. Before they close for Christmas.


00:07:18.425 --> 00:07:24.302
I read a review of
your latest performance.


00:07:24.427 --> 00:07:27.594
You did? Where?


00:07:27.719 --> 00:07:32.510
In a newspaper in the living room.
A foreign newspaper.


00:07:32.635 --> 00:07:36.677
That was just a write-up, Dad.
Not a review.


00:07:36.802 --> 00:07:39.219
Write-up or review,


00:07:39.344 --> 00:07:43.760
it's still your first production abroad.


00:07:43.885 --> 00:07:46.802
It's a huge deal. Really.


00:07:47.427 --> 00:07:49.553
Was Tomas there?


00:07:49.678 --> 00:07:54.762
-Was Tomas there?
-He stayed home to look after the kids.


00:07:54.887 --> 00:07:58.346
Yes, I understand. But...


00:07:58.471 --> 00:08:03.054
-It's good to be here.
-Just a moment, Dad. Hello?


00:08:12.137 --> 00:08:14.222
I'm coming.


00:08:21.597 --> 00:08:25.305
It's me.
How quickly can you get to our physician?


00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:28.639
Don't ask. Come as soon as you can.


00:08:32.848 --> 00:08:35.473
-Hi.
-Hi, Tomas.


00:08:40.765 --> 00:08:44.474
I'm afraid I have bad news.
Anja's diagnosis,


00:08:44.599 --> 00:08:50.265
her lung cancer operation a year ago,
evolved the way I feared.


00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:57.265
The MRI images reveal a major tumor
surrounded by a large amount of fluid.


00:09:00.808 --> 00:09:02.683
An edema.


00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:08.059
It's most likely a secondary tumor,
a metastatic growth.


00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:16.559
It's not unusual for lung cancer
to spread to the brain like that.


00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:22.767
It's incurable.


00:09:33.017 --> 00:09:36.103
No words can express how sorry I am.


00:09:40.978 --> 00:09:44.269
Feels like I've known it for ages.


00:09:45.978 --> 00:09:49.894
You often have some premonition.


00:09:55.019 --> 00:10:00.062
Before you came, I spoke to the oncologist
on call at the Cancer Center at Ullevål.


00:10:00.187 --> 00:10:03.770
She's waiting for you
with more information.


00:10:16.563 --> 00:10:18.980
Where did you park?


00:10:23.938 --> 00:10:26.146
I don't know.


00:10:30.439 --> 00:10:35.522
How long have you felt something
was wrong without saying anything?


00:10:35.647 --> 00:10:37.814
I don't know.


00:10:39.773 --> 00:10:42.482
A couple of months, maybe.


00:10:48.232 --> 00:10:54.191
Why didn't the doctors realize
something was wrong?


00:10:54.316 --> 00:10:59.649
-Why didn't they say anything?
-You never came to the control checkups.


00:10:59.774 --> 00:11:02.816
You didn't want me to come.


00:11:05.274 --> 00:11:08.233
Said you could handle it yourself.


00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:39.651
-Was it the kids?
-I don't know. I can't read.


00:11:40.651 --> 00:11:43.110
You can't read?


00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:49.278
So you have a cohabitant, three children
and three stepchildren?


00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.737
Could you say anything about my prognosis?


00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.528
Don't you want to sit?


00:12:14.404 --> 00:12:17.113
It's too early for any prognosis.


00:12:17.238 --> 00:12:21.489
The specialists are on vacation
for the next four days.


00:12:21.614 --> 00:12:27.239
But the tumor might be in a favorable
location in terms of surgery.


00:12:27.364 --> 00:12:33.572
We don't know if it's a primary tumor,
or if it spread from your lungs.


00:12:33.697 --> 00:12:36.989
But how much time do I have
if it's spread?


00:12:37.114 --> 00:12:39.948
I can't give you an answer.


00:12:41.615 --> 00:12:47.281
Initially you'll receive medication.
The edema, the fluid around the tumor,


00:12:47.406 --> 00:12:53.241
is so large that you'll need high doses
of steroids to avoid brain death.


00:12:53.366 --> 00:12:59.241
The medication, Medrol, will relieve
the swelling and the pressure.


00:12:59.366 --> 00:13:05.325
But if your headache, nausea
or visual impairment increases,


00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.117
you'll have to be admitted.


00:13:08.242 --> 00:13:11.700
I want to stay home.
I was in hospital last Christmas.


00:13:11.825 --> 00:13:15.575
-Don't want my kids to hate the holidays.
-I understand.


00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:19.742
But if it gets too difficult,
you need to call us.


00:13:20.533 --> 00:13:24.743
I don't advise you
to read about the side effects.


00:13:24.868 --> 00:13:30.034
Just remember that some people experience
a kind of high with lots of energy.


00:13:30.159 --> 00:13:35.660
While others get irritable and impatient.
It varies from person to person.


00:13:35.785 --> 00:13:37.785
Excuse me.


00:13:40.452 --> 00:13:42.369
Julie.


00:13:45.035 --> 00:13:46.910
Hi.


00:13:47.952 --> 00:13:50.369
We're just shopping.


00:13:52.785 --> 00:13:57.620
Could you make sure Grandpa
gets something to eat? Yes.


00:13:57.745 --> 00:14:03.079
And could you empty the laundry
and put in a new load?


00:14:04.412 --> 00:14:07.662
Yes. Okay. Thanks. See you.


00:14:09.912 --> 00:14:12.496
-What is it?
-Nothing.


00:14:12.621 --> 00:14:17.371
Excuse me? I recommend that you
take the first dose right away.


00:14:19.704 --> 00:14:22.287
And here's your medication.


00:14:34.039 --> 00:14:38.331
-What do we tell the kids?
-Nothing.


00:14:40.623 --> 00:14:45.539
Not until we have some answers,
know more about what to expect.


00:14:47.998 --> 00:14:50.456
What about your father?


00:15:19.709 --> 00:15:22.167
-Mom? Mom?
-Yes?


00:15:22.292 --> 00:15:25.167
-Did you find it?
-Yes.


00:15:27.542 --> 00:15:30.292
-Here.
-Thank you.


00:15:30.417 --> 00:15:33.917
Alright? Ready?


00:15:34.042 --> 00:15:36.252
Can you reach it?


00:15:36.377 --> 00:15:38.418
There!


00:15:38.543 --> 00:15:41.210
Oops!


00:15:42.793 --> 00:15:45.294
-Toddy.
-Great!


00:15:48.544 --> 00:15:51.003
-I'll have one.
-Nice!


00:15:51.128 --> 00:15:54.586
-No. Not for you, young lady.
-I'm sixteen.


00:15:54.711 --> 00:15:57.628
-Exactly. Here you go.
-Fine.


00:16:01.836 --> 00:16:06.128
How old is that Belgian girl who's coming?


00:16:06.253 --> 00:16:11.130
She's a little older than you.
Maybe eleven. Isn't that exciting?


00:16:12.505 --> 00:16:16.088
I've invited a Belgian producer
and his daughter.


00:16:16.213 --> 00:16:18.546
Have you lost your mind?


00:16:18.671 --> 00:16:23.921
-We always have an open door at Christmas.
-You could have asked.


00:16:25.588 --> 00:16:28.005
You were away.


00:16:39.631 --> 00:16:43.882
-Extra toddy for the kitchen assistant?
-Thank you.


00:16:49.965 --> 00:16:55.507
Don't you understand? I'm not ready
to meet new people right now.


00:16:57.590 --> 00:16:59.632
Okay.


00:17:10.549 --> 00:17:12.883
When I'm gone...


00:17:16.884 --> 00:17:19.134
What?


00:17:20.967 --> 00:17:24.800
When I'm gone,
I want you to find someone new.


00:17:27.134 --> 00:17:29.259
I mean it.


00:17:30.593 --> 00:17:34.510
I don't think the kids
will make it with you alone.


00:17:36.926 --> 00:17:40.051
Just promise me you'll find someone.


00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:36.055
Christmas Eve


00:19:01.807 --> 00:19:06.224
-Haven't you slept at all?
-No. I'm too nauseous.


00:19:10.057 --> 00:19:13.641
My entire body's tingling.
It's awful.


00:19:16.225 --> 00:19:21.058
-Do you want to call the hospital?
-What? No.


00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:29.809
I thought I'd buy those last presents
and get some groceries. You should rest.


00:19:30.726 --> 00:19:34.976
I want us to have a real Christmas.
I'm not tired.


00:19:51.227 --> 00:19:54.060
Has everyone tidied their rooms?


00:20:15.187 --> 00:20:17.604
Have you tidied up?


00:20:35.606 --> 00:20:40.981
I hate it!
Can you please pull yourself together?


00:20:42.564 --> 00:20:47.814
-You never do any housework!
-Erlend and I have to do everything!


00:20:47.939 --> 00:20:52.773
-Can you stop that and help me instead?
-He never does his share!


00:20:52.898 --> 00:20:56.689
-Come on, you guys. It's Christmas Eve.
-Jesus!


00:20:56.814 --> 00:21:01.857
Isak doesn't do anything, Mom!
He's turning into a spoiled brat.


00:21:01.982 --> 00:21:04.900
He isn't three anymore. He's nine.


00:21:05.025 --> 00:21:07.608
I'm ten.


00:21:07.733 --> 00:21:12.525
Okay, I'll try to shape up.
Now could you please tidy your rooms?


00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:19.608
God, I can't wait to move out.


00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:23.233
Mom...


00:21:24.858 --> 00:21:27.400
Mom!


00:21:27.525 --> 00:21:33.026
Promise me you'll never start smoking.
I won't let you. Promise me.


00:21:33.151 --> 00:21:37.110
-Okay? Don't lie to me!
-I don't. You don't get it.


00:21:37.235 --> 00:21:39.402
Stop lying!


00:21:39.527 --> 00:21:42.985
I was a damn fool.
You don't have to be.


00:21:59.028 --> 00:22:01.861
You're a godsend, Isak.


00:22:02.986 --> 00:22:05.444
Did you know that?


00:22:08.486 --> 00:22:13.029
-How many wine glasses do you need?
-For everyone. Nine.


00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:21.530
-Aren't those Belgians coming after all?
-No.


00:22:21.655 --> 00:22:24.946
-They aren't coming?
-Where are they going?


00:22:25.071 --> 00:22:28.655
-To Dag and Eline, I think.
-Who's that?


00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:32.655
-The theater manager.
-I see.


00:22:34.030 --> 00:22:39.030
-But they don't have kids.
-And they're dull as hell.


00:22:39.155 --> 00:22:43.489
Yes, why couldn't they come to us?


00:22:45.364 --> 00:22:47.281
Well, I don't know.


00:22:47.406 --> 00:22:50.157
Maybe...


00:22:50.282 --> 00:22:53.823
Maybe it's too much for them.
Many new faces.


00:22:53.948 --> 00:22:57.907
Your dad doesn't know them
that well either.


00:22:58.865 --> 00:23:01.740
Did you say they couldn't come?


00:23:03.948 --> 00:23:06.323
That's really mean.


00:23:26.117 --> 00:23:28.200
Mom?


00:23:31.742 --> 00:23:33.950
Mom?


00:24:13.412 --> 00:24:15.578
Anja!


00:24:17.162 --> 00:24:19.662
Are you there?


00:24:26.204 --> 00:24:28.621
May I come in?


00:24:29.788 --> 00:24:31.871
Please?


00:24:42.580 --> 00:24:45.080
I can't keep it a secret.


00:24:48.205 --> 00:24:54.331
You don't have to love me just because I'm
dying. But I need to know you'll help me.


00:25:09.582 --> 00:25:12.999
We're useless at sticking together.


00:25:13.124 --> 00:25:15.499
We always have been.


00:25:21.207 --> 00:25:25.207
We couldn't even stick together
when times were good.


00:25:32.834 --> 00:25:37.459
I don't want the kids to remember us
like this when I'm gone.


00:25:38.709 --> 00:25:42.501
Like I remember my parents,
and you remember yours.


00:25:43.668 --> 00:25:47.584
I want to give them
something else to believe in.


00:26:01.711 --> 00:26:06.170
I can't do it on my own.
You have to help me.


00:26:12.461 --> 00:26:16.628
-Get out!
-We just need a breather.


00:26:16.753 --> 00:26:20.587
-Get out of the couch, I said!
-Do we have to?


00:26:20.712 --> 00:26:23.421
Yes, Julie. For once in your life.


00:26:24.712 --> 00:26:30.212
My god, we've never been to church
on Christmas Eve before. What about Simon?


00:26:30.337 --> 00:26:34.297
-He's an atheist. You can't force him.
-Atheist or not.


00:26:34.422 --> 00:26:37.630
Get out if you want dinner later.


00:26:37.755 --> 00:26:40.588
-Grandpa's waiting.
-Okay.


00:26:47.131 --> 00:26:52.548
Am I speaking with the oncologist on duty?
Yes, I'm a patient.


00:26:52.673 --> 00:26:55.256
Anja Richter.


00:27:00.048 --> 00:27:04.881
I'm afraid.
My head feels like it's about to explode.


00:27:06.757 --> 00:27:09.924
No, I've never had anxiety like this.


00:27:13.008 --> 00:27:16.258
I'm nauseous absolutely all the time.


00:27:16.800 --> 00:27:20.216
I've got relentless stomach cramps.


00:27:21.300 --> 00:27:24.550
And I can't sleep at all.


00:27:26.841 --> 00:27:29.425
No, I don't want to go to hospital.


00:27:29.550 --> 00:27:33.341
But I don't know how long
I can go on pretending.


00:27:33.466 --> 00:27:40.052
Is there anyone there in the meantime
who can help me break it to the children?


00:27:40.177 --> 00:27:42.427
Yes?


00:28:01.718 --> 00:28:04.343
-How do you feel?
-Blind.


00:28:17.679 --> 00:28:20.179
-You look nice.
-Thanks.


00:28:41.846 --> 00:28:45.264
No, no, no. Put it away.


00:28:45.389 --> 00:28:49.639
Wait. Take the starters.
It'll be ready in a moment.


00:28:49.764 --> 00:28:54.139
I just need a tiny piece of ham.
It's just decor, right?


00:28:54.264 --> 00:28:57.931
-Dad?
-Grandpa?


00:28:58.056 --> 00:29:02.390
-So tell me, how was church?
-The sermon was ridiculous.


00:29:02.515 --> 00:29:05.765
So farfetched it was almost funny.


00:29:05.890 --> 00:29:11.640
-I just recruited an atheist! Any others?
-Poor preacher. She was so nervous.


00:29:11.765 --> 00:29:15.557
No wonder, with that bowl haircut.


00:29:17.558 --> 00:29:22.516
-I don't think it'll become a tradition.
-Probably not.


00:29:22.641 --> 00:29:25.725
Here's to Christmas... and Grandpa!


00:29:25.850 --> 00:29:28.975
Cheers!


00:29:29.100 --> 00:29:31.642
Merry Christmas!


00:29:33.892 --> 00:29:36.434
And here's to Anja.


00:29:38.684 --> 00:29:41.642
Back in great shape. Cheers.


00:29:42.517 --> 00:29:45.892
-Cheers!
-Cheers, Mom!


00:29:56.144 --> 00:30:00.519
-We want everyone in the picture.
-Make room for Grandpa.


00:30:02.102 --> 00:30:06.477
-Come here.
-Mom will sit there. Just move over there.


00:30:07.477 --> 00:30:10.352
-Sit down as well, Tomas.
-No.


00:30:10.477 --> 00:30:14.394
You sit in the middle.
I'll take care of it.


00:30:14.519 --> 00:30:17.061
Sit in the middle.


00:30:19.312 --> 00:30:22.187
Looks great. Let me see...


00:30:23.271 --> 00:30:27.063
-A, F, E...
-May I?


00:30:27.188 --> 00:30:31.396
-You sure are bossy, Martin.
-True enough.


00:30:31.521 --> 00:30:34.646
Sit next to Anja, okay?


00:30:38.521 --> 00:30:40.771
Everyone ready?


00:30:42.063 --> 00:30:45.147
Five, four, two, three!


00:30:45.939 --> 00:30:48.564
One!


00:30:48.689 --> 00:30:50.772
Smile.


00:30:59.023 --> 00:31:02.815
Well, there's one last present. No card.


00:31:02.940 --> 00:31:05.106
It's for Mom.


00:31:09.231 --> 00:31:11.607
-Can I open it?
-Sure.


00:31:25.107 --> 00:31:27.524
"India"?


00:31:32.817 --> 00:31:35.400
It says you're getting


00:31:35.525 --> 00:31:38.359
a trip to India.


00:31:38.484 --> 00:31:40.776
-From Dad.
-Wow.


00:31:40.901 --> 00:31:45.568
-Haven't you always wanted to go there?
-Yes.


00:31:45.693 --> 00:31:49.859
-Can I come with you? As your Sherpa?
-Nice move, Erlend.


00:31:49.984 --> 00:31:52.484
So it'll be you and Mom?


00:31:52.609 --> 00:31:55.818
Are you going together, or...?


00:31:55.943 --> 00:31:58.818
Well, that's up to her.


00:31:58.943 --> 00:32:01.651
What's a Sherpa?


00:32:01.777 --> 00:32:04.403
It's like a tour guide.


00:32:07.236 --> 00:32:09.653
Are you coming?


00:32:15.986 --> 00:32:17.861
Dad? My turn.


00:32:17.986 --> 00:32:20.195
No, no, no!


00:32:26.403 --> 00:32:29.195
You're nuts! No!


00:32:29.320 --> 00:32:32.779
-Come on, Mom!
-Mom, come!


00:32:32.904 --> 00:32:35.738
-No, Mom!
-No!


00:32:38.697 --> 00:32:41.072
I'll throw up!


00:32:41.197 --> 00:32:44.947
-Hey, come on, Grandpa!
-Nope.


00:33:01.448 --> 00:33:03.448
Here.


00:33:03.573 --> 00:33:06.739
Do you have everything you need?


00:33:06.864 --> 00:33:12.657
-Was your evening as good as mine?
-It was a lovely Christmas Eve.


00:33:12.782 --> 00:33:16.074
-But...
-Goodnight, Dad.


00:33:16.199 --> 00:33:19.324
Are the two of you struggling?


00:33:19.449 --> 00:33:24.158
I do wish that you and Tomas


00:33:24.283 --> 00:33:26.991
were happier together.


00:33:32.116 --> 00:33:36.366
We do what we like.
What we do best. We work.


00:33:36.491 --> 00:33:39.033
At least I try to work.


00:33:40.451 --> 00:33:43.409
I guess we're as happy as we deserve.


00:33:43.534 --> 00:33:45.826
Well, Anja...


00:33:46.992 --> 00:33:52.035
You choose the life you get
to a great degree.


00:33:57.535 --> 00:34:00.910
I'll never be able to go to India.


00:34:03.243 --> 00:34:05.993
You don't know that yet.


00:34:06.118 --> 00:34:09.243
I can't even read about India.


00:34:10.743 --> 00:34:13.160
I can read for you.


00:34:16.120 --> 00:34:18.787
I had this great-aunt.


00:34:20.787 --> 00:34:23.162
She used to tell her husband:


00:34:23.287 --> 00:34:27.662
"When one of us dies,
I'm going to travel the world!"


00:34:38.162 --> 00:34:43.788
Have you never imagined
I could die before you?


00:34:49.372 --> 00:34:51.497
Of course I have.


00:34:56.289 --> 00:34:59.664
Christmas Day


00:35:23.541 --> 00:35:27.666
Yes, I'm excited.
It'll be fun.


00:35:29.374 --> 00:35:33.958
No, me first. It's my turn!


00:35:36.542 --> 00:35:39.209
Isak! Come in! Ready to party?


00:35:39.334 --> 00:35:43.084
Hi, Erlend. Hi, Leif Martin.


00:35:43.209 --> 00:35:47.500
We followed the sound of Christmas carols.


00:35:48.625 --> 00:35:50.834
Thanks. Hi.


00:35:50.959 --> 00:35:53.585
-Survived Christmas?
-Yes. Did you?


00:35:53.710 --> 00:35:56.918
I'm okay, but Arthur and Christmas...


00:35:57.043 --> 00:35:59.751
I love Christmas.


00:35:59.876 --> 00:36:04.336
You can hang it there.
Congratulations on the great reviews!


00:36:11.336 --> 00:36:15.086
We won't stay if it's too much for you.


00:36:15.211 --> 00:36:19.419
If it gets tough,
we'll stick together.


00:36:19.544 --> 00:36:23.669
-Okay. Go on in. I need to take my Medrol.
-Are you sure?


00:36:23.794 --> 00:36:26.878
Yes, I won't be long.


00:36:50.004 --> 00:36:52.379
They're dying of thirst.


00:36:54.964 --> 00:36:57.505
Did you see the doctor?


00:36:57.630 --> 00:37:02.048
-Should I be worried? Everything okay?
-Yes.


00:37:02.173 --> 00:37:06.006
That's great. You see? Hey...


00:37:06.131 --> 00:37:08.881
Your father is so proud of you.


00:37:09.006 --> 00:37:13.215
Really. But you haven't told him
anything about the show.


00:37:13.340 --> 00:37:18.840
Not Tomas either. I told him everything.
About the festival invitations.


00:37:18.965 --> 00:37:25.132
The grant for the new project.
They're so proud of you, both of them.


00:37:25.257 --> 00:37:28.341
Why haven't you told them? Huh?


00:37:32.592 --> 00:37:35.092
Thanks.


00:37:35.217 --> 00:37:38.217
-Come on. Vera's waiting.
-I'm coming.


00:37:55.551 --> 00:37:58.759
-Anja!
-Hi.


00:37:58.884 --> 00:38:03.552
Oh gosh. What is it about me
that turns Pollock on?


00:38:03.677 --> 00:38:05.719
You're in heat.


00:38:05.844 --> 00:38:10.677
You're embarrassing me.
Stop it!


00:38:10.802 --> 00:38:13.760
-How was Amsterdam?
-Great.


00:38:13.885 --> 00:38:16.053
Let's go outside. Come.


00:38:25.345 --> 00:38:27.345
Oh my god!


00:38:27.470 --> 00:38:31.470
If only that mutt Pollock
had been human,


00:38:31.595 --> 00:38:33.803
there'd be hope for me too.


00:38:33.928 --> 00:38:37.721
I can't find anyone who's single.


00:38:37.846 --> 00:38:41.847
They're either married, gay or minors.


00:38:44.055 --> 00:38:47.597
Enough about me.
Tell me about Amsterdam.


00:38:51.930 --> 00:38:54.013
It's spread.


00:38:57.472 --> 00:39:00.013
To the brain. It's incurable.


00:39:03.638 --> 00:39:08.223
My doctor says I should pray
for a miracle. No one survives.


00:39:10.890 --> 00:39:13.807
We'll know more in a couple of days.


00:39:17.849 --> 00:39:20.474
-Can't they do anything?
-No.


00:39:24.557 --> 00:39:27.182
You sure?


00:39:27.307 --> 00:39:29.140
Pretty much.


00:39:29.265 --> 00:39:35.183
They just don't dare say so until all
the specialists have examined the images.


00:39:49.851 --> 00:39:51.809
Jesus Christ.


00:39:51.934 --> 00:39:54.517
It's so unfair.


00:39:55.892 --> 00:39:59.017
If it had only... been me.


00:40:00.393 --> 00:40:02.768
Or Arthur or Tomas.


00:40:04.352 --> 00:40:06.935
I don't have kids.


00:40:09.018 --> 00:40:13.185
You've been alone with everything.
Tomas, he...


00:40:15.186 --> 00:40:18.644
-The kids need you more than him.
-Don't say that.


00:40:18.769 --> 00:40:22.769
-Just when it's your turn to...
-Stop it, Vera.


00:40:39.354 --> 00:40:41.770
What can I do?


00:40:43.145 --> 00:40:46.187
For you? For all of you?


00:40:51.896 --> 00:40:54.272
I don't know.


00:40:54.397 --> 00:40:57.856
I don't even know how to tell the kids.


00:41:00.772 --> 00:41:03.522
Only you and Tomas know.


00:41:03.647 --> 00:41:07.981
What does he say?
How's he taking it?


00:41:09.356 --> 00:41:11.189
I don't know.


00:41:16.606 --> 00:41:19.314
I haven't asked.


00:41:30.274 --> 00:41:34.524
I thought it was supposed to be a secret?


00:41:35.774 --> 00:41:38.566
Does Arthur know as well?


00:41:40.274 --> 00:41:42.108
No.


00:41:42.233 --> 00:41:45.774
It isn't always easy to help you, Anja.


00:44:11.410 --> 00:44:13.452
Anja...


00:44:14.535 --> 00:44:16.535
Anja.


00:44:16.660 --> 00:44:20.369
Anja! Anja!


00:44:20.494 --> 00:44:22.535
Anja!


00:44:50.162 --> 00:44:52.247
There.


00:45:00.080 --> 00:45:03.955
Second day of Christmas


00:45:05.163 --> 00:45:08.872
-Thanks for now.
-Let me take your suitcase.


00:45:08.997 --> 00:45:11.248
I can cope.


00:45:12.331 --> 00:45:16.414
I'm no use if I can't even
carry my own suitcase.


00:45:16.539 --> 00:45:18.624
No.


00:45:31.582 --> 00:45:37.290
-Thanks. I'm going to the airport express.
-I'll get the door for you.


00:45:37.415 --> 00:45:40.124
-Have a nice trip!
-Thank you.


00:46:08.626 --> 00:46:11.168
What are you doing?


00:46:12.918 --> 00:46:18.294
-Are the boys asleep?
-Yes, in front of a bad Christmas movie.


00:46:23.336 --> 00:46:25.544
You can go to bed.


00:46:25.669 --> 00:46:28.711
I'll stay up until Julie comes home.


00:46:29.711 --> 00:46:33.628
No, I can't sleep anyway. I can stay up.


00:46:34.711 --> 00:46:37.587
Oh, I hate Medrol!


00:46:37.712 --> 00:46:41.795
I feel so high.
Like I'll never come back down.


00:46:50.505 --> 00:46:53.671
-It's so weird.
-What is?


00:46:53.796 --> 00:46:57.546
Before, if I tried to describe my life...


00:46:59.046 --> 00:47:03.255
My memories were never
in the right order, like...


00:47:03.380 --> 00:47:09.339
They were always tied to places I'd lived,
boyfriends I'd had, dance projects,


00:47:09.464 --> 00:47:12.714
journeys, childbirths, deaths.


00:47:16.672 --> 00:47:19.631
But I never remembered
what the years were.


00:47:19.756 --> 00:47:23.715
But now, when I see the end...


00:47:23.840 --> 00:47:27.257
My life's laid out in chronological order.


00:47:29.173 --> 00:47:31.466
Almost like...


00:47:31.591 --> 00:47:37.299
A PowerPoint presentation
with a graphic timeline.


00:47:37.424 --> 00:47:40.758
Where the middle of my life is like...


00:47:40.883 --> 00:47:46.466
It looks like this thick gray graph


00:47:46.591 --> 00:47:49.174
of postpartum apathy.


00:47:55.800 --> 00:47:59.593
So how do I feature in the graphics?


00:48:01.593 --> 00:48:05.135
-Like a dot?
-No.


00:48:07.051 --> 00:48:09.760
Like many dots.


00:48:09.885 --> 00:48:12.718
Coming and going on the timeline.


00:48:17.301 --> 00:48:20.093
Right. Uplifting.


00:48:24.636 --> 00:48:28.136
Julie? Hi.


00:48:28.262 --> 00:48:30.178
Hi.


00:48:30.928 --> 00:48:33.595
Are you okay?


00:48:33.720 --> 00:48:35.720
Sure.


00:48:35.845 --> 00:48:38.595
What are you doing here?


00:48:41.387 --> 00:48:46.887
Hi. Why are you home so early?
Wasn't it any fun?


00:48:47.012 --> 00:48:50.554
Oh, sure.
It was fun.


00:48:53.304 --> 00:48:56.054
I really have to pee.


00:49:08.347 --> 00:49:11.597
-It's not the first time.
-Oh, hush.


00:49:11.722 --> 00:49:14.180
She's adventurous.


00:49:15.430 --> 00:49:18.098
Lusts for life. Like you.


00:49:20.473 --> 00:49:23.890
She's got you under her thumb.


00:49:24.015 --> 00:49:26.015
Yes.


00:49:27.140 --> 00:49:30.306
Promise me you'll take good care of her.


00:49:33.681 --> 00:49:35.641
I will.


00:49:35.766 --> 00:49:37.932
December 27


00:49:38.057 --> 00:49:41.099
I'll be there as soon as I can. Okay, bye.


00:49:41.224 --> 00:49:43.892
-Yes?
-The images from Aleris.


00:49:44.017 --> 00:49:48.683
Thank you. The team
will review them tomorrow morning.


00:49:48.808 --> 00:49:55.183
We need some advice about what to tell
the children. We need to prepare them.


00:49:55.308 --> 00:49:59.642
Yes, it says so in your medical record.
It's not a good time.


00:49:59.767 --> 00:50:03.517
The specialist nurse
won't be back until January.


00:50:03.642 --> 00:50:06.558
Titles aren't that important.


00:50:08.684 --> 00:50:13.602
Yes? I'm on my way. I see.
Like I said, I'm sorry.


00:50:13.727 --> 00:50:18.435
-Is there no one here with experience?
-Not during the holidays.


00:50:18.560 --> 00:50:23.185
Don't people die during the holidays?
Do you ask them to wait?


00:50:23.310 --> 00:50:28.102
I'm sure you see the challenge,
with so many children involved.


00:50:28.227 --> 00:50:33.144
Not getting any certainty, no help.
Someone must be qualified.


00:50:33.269 --> 00:50:37.103
-Not like that. We're specialized.
-But you are human?


00:50:37.228 --> 00:50:41.104
Don't you have any experience
with next of kin?


00:50:41.229 --> 00:50:45.729
I realize this is difficult.
We've made out a prescription


00:50:45.854 --> 00:50:49.021
for sleeping pills and a sedative.


00:50:49.146 --> 00:50:52.854
It'll help you relax. Okay? I'm sorry.


00:51:00.979 --> 00:51:06.688
Hi. Welcome to Hospice Lovisenberg.
My name is Bente, I'm a nurse.


00:51:06.813 --> 00:51:10.938
-Hi.
-Hi. Welcome. Let's go in there.


00:51:17.856 --> 00:51:22.481
Well, my advice is to not shield
the children from the truth.


00:51:22.606 --> 00:51:28.064
But try to convey it to them according to
their age and maturity.


00:51:28.189 --> 00:51:33.649
Your children won't be as vulnerable
as the children you have together.


00:51:33.774 --> 00:51:36.940
Because they'll still have a mother.


00:51:37.065 --> 00:51:41.649
Anja has taken responsibility for
my three oldest children too.


00:51:41.774 --> 00:51:45.149
She's a key part of their lives, it's...


00:51:45.274 --> 00:51:50.525
Tomas. That's not how it works.
The youngest kids will lose their mother.


00:51:50.650 --> 00:51:55.484
They're all I think about
and care about protecting right now.


00:51:55.609 --> 00:52:01.276
You always expected me to feel and act
the same way to your kids as to our kids.


00:52:01.401 --> 00:52:05.984
Not just treat them equally,
but feel equally about all of them.


00:52:06.109 --> 00:52:11.984
I always thought it was the natural thing,
that I was unnatural and heartless.


00:52:12.109 --> 00:52:16.567
It's never been clearer to me
how misguided I was.


00:52:16.692 --> 00:52:19.527
I've always loved my own more.


00:52:58.946 --> 00:53:03.238
It's like we're at work together.
In a whole new field.


00:53:06.238 --> 00:53:11.446
-This doesn't look like a hospital.
-That's what you said last Christmas.


00:53:11.571 --> 00:53:17.531
I often say you should give children
10 % more hope than you have yourself.


00:53:18.572 --> 00:53:24.365
Not matter what age, you should never
take their hope away.


00:53:24.490 --> 00:53:29.240
-But I haven't been given any hope.
-We don't know that for sure.


00:53:29.365 --> 00:53:32.573
They say it's probably a metastatic tumor.


00:53:32.698 --> 00:53:36.615
It's incurable,
but they hope it's operable.


00:53:36.740 --> 00:53:38.823
Okay. Good.


00:53:38.948 --> 00:53:44.408
And they have highly competent
neurosurgeons at Ullevål.


00:53:44.533 --> 00:53:49.533
And all statistics
should be read with caution.


00:53:49.658 --> 00:53:51.366
Meaning?


00:53:51.491 --> 00:53:55.033
A patient with lung cancer
and brain metastasis


00:53:55.158 --> 00:53:59.825
has little chance of survival
in statistical terms.


00:53:59.950 --> 00:54:04.200
But in my three decades in the field,
I've seen patients


00:54:04.325 --> 00:54:07.951
who have survived brain metastases.


00:54:08.076 --> 00:54:13.118
They're just too few to show up
in the cancer statistics.


00:54:13.243 --> 00:54:15.826
How many?


00:54:16.660 --> 00:54:19.701
I can count them on one hand.


00:54:31.744 --> 00:54:34.828
Can I really just call him at home?


00:54:36.828 --> 00:54:40.453
Wouldn't I be jumping in line?


00:54:41.995 --> 00:54:45.828
This isn't a good time
to be politically correct.


00:54:53.870 --> 00:54:57.203
-Do you want me to call him?
-No.


00:54:57.328 --> 00:55:00.163
That wouldn't be right.


00:55:00.288 --> 00:55:02.955
I've made a few calls, asked around.


00:55:03.080 --> 00:55:08.622
He's said to be the best neurosurgeon,
not just at Ullevål, but in Norway.


00:55:14.539 --> 00:55:18.247
-Okay, I'll do it. But I want to be alone.
-Okay.


00:55:18.372 --> 00:55:20.872
I'll wait outside.


00:55:20.997 --> 00:55:23.580
Can I borrow your eyes first?


00:55:33.873 --> 00:55:35.832
Good luck.


00:55:48.707 --> 00:55:51.416
Hi.


00:55:51.541 --> 00:55:56.375
You don't know who I am.
My name is Anja Richter.


00:55:57.500 --> 00:56:00.167
Am I interrupting anything?


00:56:00.292 --> 00:56:02.750
Right. Okay.


00:56:02.875 --> 00:56:06.417
I'm a patient at Ullevål
in a difficult situation.


00:56:34.377 --> 00:56:39.669
He was at a Christmas party, but
will perform the surgery if it's possible.


00:56:58.212 --> 00:57:01.337
I mean it. That's enough.


00:57:03.254 --> 00:57:05.754
There. Stay down.


00:57:08.879 --> 00:57:11.087
They're waiting for us.


00:57:12.337 --> 00:57:16.256
Dad, Mom's tired of us
always being late, and...


00:57:16.381 --> 00:57:20.131
Everyone has to be here.
Just tell her


00:57:20.256 --> 00:57:23.423
that it's a family crisis.


00:57:27.548 --> 00:57:31.089
-You're breaking up?
-No.


00:57:32.131 --> 00:57:35.256
No, Ada. We're not breaking up.


00:57:53.091 --> 00:57:56.133
-Who should start?
-I'll do it.


00:57:56.258 --> 00:57:58.341
Okay.


00:57:59.675 --> 00:58:01.758
Good.


00:58:10.926 --> 00:58:13.342
Gather around the couch.


00:58:24.177 --> 00:58:26.760
Right, Anja...


00:58:28.177 --> 00:58:32.719
-Are we having a family council?
-Sort of.


00:58:37.136 --> 00:58:42.969
I've been informed that I have
a tumor in my brain.


00:58:45.969 --> 00:58:50.511
It's most likely spread from my lungs.


00:58:53.470 --> 00:58:59.680
The good news is that the tumor is seated
where they think it might be operable.


00:59:03.305 --> 00:59:07.055
Well, they say it's serious, but...


00:59:07.180 --> 00:59:10.680
We still don't know what
the outcome will be.


00:59:10.805 --> 00:59:14.805
We'll find out more
at the hospital tomorrow.


00:59:20.513 --> 00:59:23.763
They're going to operate on your head?


00:59:30.557 --> 00:59:33.390
Inside your brain?


00:59:33.515 --> 00:59:36.348
Yes, maybe.


00:59:36.473 --> 00:59:43.057
The good news is that if they do operate,
I'll have the best surgeon in the country.


00:59:45.682 --> 00:59:48.057
But...


00:59:48.182 --> 00:59:52.599
Last Christmas you told us
that everything would be okay.


00:59:54.558 --> 00:59:58.016
Everyone thought so.
The doctors as well.


00:59:58.141 --> 01:00:01.767
But despite that, this happened.


01:00:02.934 --> 01:00:08.434
We spoke to a doctor today
who knew of several similar cases


01:00:08.559 --> 01:00:11.350
that had gone well.


01:00:11.475 --> 01:00:15.225
-Were there many?
-Quite a few.


01:00:22.643 --> 01:00:25.351
The milk.


01:00:57.228 --> 01:01:00.103
-Bye.
-Goodbye.


01:01:02.437 --> 01:01:04.520
Bye.


01:01:43.191 --> 01:01:45.607
I'm sorry.


01:01:47.857 --> 01:01:50.191
Sorry for what?


01:01:51.816 --> 01:01:54.316
Sorry for being so mean.


01:01:57.024 --> 01:02:00.399
You have nothing to apologize for.


01:02:01.691 --> 01:02:04.525
-I do.
-No.


01:02:09.400 --> 01:02:11.484
Sure?


01:02:12.776 --> 01:02:15.151
Absolutely sure.


01:02:26.776 --> 01:02:30.735
-I'll never forgive myself.
-For what?


01:02:32.110 --> 01:02:35.694
-For being a smoker.
-Don't say that.


01:02:38.902 --> 01:02:41.944
No one knows
that that's the reason.


01:02:42.069 --> 01:02:46.278
-But I know.
-Stop torturing yourself.


01:02:52.111 --> 01:02:54.570
What are you taking?


01:02:55.986 --> 01:02:59.487
Vival and Imovane...


01:03:05.737 --> 01:03:09.112
December 28


01:03:09.237 --> 01:03:14.112
I brought some extra clothes just in case.


01:03:14.237 --> 01:03:18.905
And some proper coffee.
I don't really like that instant stuff.


01:03:19.030 --> 01:03:23.114
-Where are the kids?
-They're still sleeping.


01:03:42.739 --> 01:03:47.989
-Nothing eases the nausea except food.
-It's the medication, steroids.


01:03:48.114 --> 01:03:52.866
-The same stuff they give to anorectics.
-How do you know?


01:03:52.991 --> 01:03:56.200
My new online friend, PubMed.com.


01:03:56.325 --> 01:03:58.908
Good morning.


01:03:59.033 --> 01:04:00.991
Hi.


01:04:01.991 --> 01:04:04.325
Good morning.


01:04:07.616 --> 01:04:09.991
Good morning.


01:04:10.116 --> 01:04:14.866
We're going to the hospital.
Vera will stay here with you.


01:04:15.741 --> 01:04:18.617
Hi. Good morning.


01:04:30.577 --> 01:04:32.785
Knut Åsdam?


01:04:37.285 --> 01:04:41.243
Hi. I'm Dr. Thea Falkentorp.
Please come with me.


01:04:51.119 --> 01:04:56.412
I realize that you're anxious,
so I'll get straight to the point.


01:04:56.537 --> 01:05:03.120
The specialists have held a meeting
and studied your MRI images.


01:05:03.245 --> 01:05:10.080
We've given your brain surgery top
priority and scheduled it on 2 January.


01:05:10.205 --> 01:05:13.038
In five days.


01:05:13.163 --> 01:05:17.580
I understand you've contacted
a surgeon here at the hospital,


01:05:17.705 --> 01:05:21.413
and that he's agreed
to perform the surgery.


01:05:24.788 --> 01:05:28.831
The images also show that the tumor


01:05:28.956 --> 01:05:33.622
is a metastasis from the lungs.


01:05:34.706 --> 01:05:37.457
That makes it incurable.


01:05:49.832 --> 01:05:52.957
So how much time do I have left?


01:05:54.415 --> 01:05:59.998
It's very hard to determine.
Cancer is like peeling an onion.


01:06:00.123 --> 01:06:02.209
-An onion?
-Yes.


01:06:02.334 --> 01:06:08.167
The picture is complicated.
It depends on the outcome of the surgery.


01:06:08.292 --> 01:06:11.709
The result of the CAT scan
of your lungs today


01:06:11.834 --> 01:06:17.084
will reveal whether it's spread
to other organs in the body.


01:06:17.209 --> 01:06:21.334
They'll determine your treatment
moving forward.


01:06:24.209 --> 01:06:28.710
Could you be more specific?
This isn't just about me.


01:06:30.335 --> 01:06:33.293
I need to...


01:06:33.418 --> 01:06:39.294
I need to know the worst possible outcome
to find out how to prepare the children.


01:06:40.419 --> 01:06:42.586
Anja...


01:06:42.711 --> 01:06:46.169
All cancer patients are different.


01:06:46.294 --> 01:06:52.169
There are some who refuse to face reality.
It's too exhausting.


01:06:52.294 --> 01:06:56.920
Fine, but I want to know.
How much time do I have left?


01:06:59.837 --> 01:07:03.628
In the worst case,
I'd say three months.


01:07:03.753 --> 01:07:08.463
But we hope the operation
will give you more than that.


01:07:17.796 --> 01:07:20.796
Is the operation itself dangerous?


01:07:20.921 --> 01:07:25.797
All operations involve a certain risk,
brain surgery in particular.


01:07:25.922 --> 01:07:30.714
The surgeon is more qualified
to answer that question.


01:07:35.255 --> 01:07:38.755
Can you get married before the surgery?


01:07:41.340 --> 01:07:43.631
Married? Well, yes.


01:07:43.756 --> 01:07:49.591
We do have a hospital chaplain
who can perform weddings.


01:07:49.716 --> 01:07:54.966
Normally, with all the paperwork,
I'm not sure it would be possible.


01:07:55.091 --> 01:07:58.007
But there's room for exceptions.


01:08:02.382 --> 01:08:05.174
Was that a proposal?


01:08:09.632 --> 01:08:13.133
I don't understand why
you want to do it now.


01:08:13.258 --> 01:08:15.968
I thought you wanted to.


01:08:16.093 --> 01:08:19.218
Years ago, sure.
But why now?


01:08:26.009 --> 01:08:28.218
It just feels...


01:08:29.301 --> 01:08:32.718
Like signing a death warrant.


01:08:36.551 --> 01:08:41.177
Otherwise we could have waited
until after the operation.


01:08:43.344 --> 01:08:48.095
It just feels right.
It's the only thing that feels right.


01:08:52.678 --> 01:08:55.428
If we're going to get married...


01:08:55.553 --> 01:08:58.761
We both have to love each other.


01:09:14.679 --> 01:09:17.429
The dentist.


01:09:19.222 --> 01:09:21.847
Hello?


01:09:23.305 --> 01:09:25.555
Right.


01:09:25.680 --> 01:09:29.597
No, I don't need an appointment.
My teeth don't matter.


01:09:29.722 --> 01:09:32.263
I have terminal cancer.


01:09:32.388 --> 01:09:35.973
You can just delete me from your list.


01:09:42.264 --> 01:09:44.264
Breathe in.


01:09:44.389 --> 01:09:47.014
Hold your breath.


01:09:48.681 --> 01:09:50.598
Breathe normally.


01:09:51.515 --> 01:09:56.515
-Can you breathe?
-It's like a burning claw around my chest.


01:09:56.640 --> 01:10:00.225
Try to breathe calmly and deeply.


01:10:00.350 --> 01:10:03.766
Breathe with your belly.


01:10:03.891 --> 01:10:07.683
Are you more relaxed now?
Breathe with your belly.


01:10:09.308 --> 01:10:13.766
It'll be fine. You can do it.
You'll get the answers you need.


01:10:13.891 --> 01:10:17.933
We'll roll you in and start.


01:10:27.893 --> 01:10:30.310
I don't know.


01:10:30.435 --> 01:10:36.852
I don't know what's the medication, what's
her fear of dying, and what's just Anja.


01:10:36.977 --> 01:10:41.560
She's so volatile and intense.


01:10:41.685 --> 01:10:47.518
As if she didn't have enough energy
to begin with. I don't know.


01:10:49.018 --> 01:10:52.852
Yes, she's here now. I have to go.


01:10:52.977 --> 01:10:55.519
I will. Bye.


01:10:57.604 --> 01:10:59.729
How did it go?


01:11:01.979 --> 01:11:05.145
Not too good?


01:11:05.270 --> 01:11:07.187
Who was that?


01:11:07.312 --> 01:11:11.729
I'm calling friends and family.
Like we agreed.


01:11:11.854 --> 01:11:13.937
That was Frans.


01:11:15.770 --> 01:11:18.604
What about Dad?


01:11:18.729 --> 01:11:22.980
He's the only one
I think you have to call yourself.


01:11:23.105 --> 01:11:25.188
I can't do it.


01:11:26.896 --> 01:11:29.271
Okay.


01:11:29.396 --> 01:11:32.189
What are people saying?


01:11:33.189 --> 01:11:36.772
Well, that they don't know what to say.


01:11:36.897 --> 01:11:40.189
They feel sorry for you and the kids.


01:11:40.814 --> 01:11:44.189
Frans told me to say he's thinking of you.


01:11:45.189 --> 01:11:50.107
-Was that all he had to say?
-No.


01:11:50.232 --> 01:11:56.440
He said he's sorry for me too,
having to take care of all the kids alone.


01:12:39.361 --> 01:12:41.486
It wasn't a problem.


01:12:41.611 --> 01:12:45.652
I managed to postpone
the production indefinitely.


01:12:47.777 --> 01:12:50.069
Hey...


01:12:50.194 --> 01:12:54.111
I need to know.
Have you been faithful?


01:12:57.319 --> 01:13:02.069
I'd like to know if there
have been others while we have...


01:13:02.194 --> 01:13:06.570
It wouldn't be a big deal,
so don't be afraid to tell me.


01:13:09.238 --> 01:13:13.238
Think of it as my last wish.
A truthful exchange.


01:13:13.363 --> 01:13:17.113
-Is this a good idea?
-Does it have to be?


01:13:26.113 --> 01:13:28.821
I had a flirt. A fling.


01:13:28.946 --> 01:13:31.947
Completely idiotic and meaningless.


01:13:32.072 --> 01:13:36.405
Quickly done and quickly forgotten.
Many years ago.


01:13:36.530 --> 01:13:39.030
During a job in Germany.


01:13:42.531 --> 01:13:44.615
I remember.


01:13:46.365 --> 01:13:49.781
Your fling sent you a present, right?


01:13:50.948 --> 01:13:55.573
The ugliest leather jacket ever.


01:13:55.698 --> 01:13:58.115
Stone-washed.


01:13:58.240 --> 01:14:00.782
She'd designed it herself.


01:14:04.074 --> 01:14:06.741
I didn't know you knew.


01:14:06.866 --> 01:14:10.282
The funny thing was,
I wasn't jealous at all.


01:14:11.199 --> 01:14:15.617
I was immersed in Julie, my baby.


01:14:18.158 --> 01:14:21.617
But what really drove me crazy
with jealously,


01:14:21.742 --> 01:14:27.368
was your work and your endless
need for acknowledgement.


01:14:27.493 --> 01:14:30.701
It's been my greatest rival.


01:14:30.826 --> 01:14:37.576
I thought it was unfair you got to work
so much, kept producing all the time.


01:14:39.534 --> 01:14:42.118
But it's no longer important.


01:14:45.493 --> 01:14:47.577
Any more?


01:14:47.702 --> 01:14:50.619
-Anything else to confess?
-No.


01:14:52.995 --> 01:14:55.620
Aren't you curious about me?


01:15:05.578 --> 01:15:08.661
I'm not sure I want to know.


01:15:09.745 --> 01:15:12.161
You can relax.


01:15:12.286 --> 01:15:15.870
I've been so faithful it's ridiculous.


01:15:15.995 --> 01:15:19.079
All I've kissed is our kids' necks.


01:15:22.580 --> 01:15:26.205
But I've seen something
much more dangerous.


01:15:26.330 --> 01:15:29.122
I fell truly in love.


01:15:30.663 --> 01:15:35.038
If I'd followed my heart,
I wouldn't have been here now.


01:15:42.747 --> 01:15:45.164
Do you regret it?


01:15:47.664 --> 01:15:49.248
No.


01:15:49.373 --> 01:15:52.289
He wouldn't have been worth it.


01:15:57.082 --> 01:15:59.999
Should we get home to the kids?


01:16:01.582 --> 01:16:03.665
Yes.


01:16:06.207 --> 01:16:08.624
One more thing.


01:16:09.707 --> 01:16:14.041
I take back what I said
about you finding someone else.


01:16:31.501 --> 01:16:33.792
Hello!


01:16:33.917 --> 01:16:36.709
Hi. Sorry we're late.


01:16:38.418 --> 01:16:43.668
-Help yourselves to some pasta.
-It was delicious.


01:16:44.752 --> 01:16:47.043
-Really.
-Thanks.


01:16:51.752 --> 01:16:53.835
How did it go?


01:16:54.918 --> 01:16:57.377
We're getting married.


01:16:59.669 --> 01:17:01.753
What happened?


01:17:02.836 --> 01:17:06.920
Anja is going to have the tumor
removed on 2 January.


01:17:07.045 --> 01:17:09.962
We have to do it before that.


01:17:10.087 --> 01:17:12.212
When?


01:17:12.337 --> 01:17:15.837
-New Year's Eve.
-Right.


01:17:18.254 --> 01:17:20.754
In three days?


01:17:20.879 --> 01:17:24.129
But that's your birthday, Mom.


01:17:24.212 --> 01:17:28.795
So it's your birthday, wedding
and New Year's Eve all in one?


01:17:29.420 --> 01:17:32.006
-That'll be great.
-But...


01:17:32.131 --> 01:17:34.839
Where will you get married?


01:17:34.964 --> 01:17:37.589
We have a hospital chaplain.


01:17:37.714 --> 01:17:42.756
But we're not sure whether we can find
a church on such short notice.


01:17:42.881 --> 01:17:48.131
-Do you have to get married in church?
-Either that, or the hospital chapel.


01:17:48.256 --> 01:17:53.131
It has to be done by a hospital chaplain
to cut through the red tape.


01:17:53.256 --> 01:17:56.965
We're not getting married in a hospital.


01:17:57.090 --> 01:18:00.798
-No.
-But we're going to have a party?


01:18:00.923 --> 01:18:03.298
Of course we'll have a party.


01:18:03.423 --> 01:18:08.299
-I don't think we'll be that many.
-Just your hundred closest friends.


01:18:08.424 --> 01:18:10.716
I know how to party.


01:18:10.841 --> 01:18:14.966
But I'm not a great organizer,
so we'll need help.


01:18:15.091 --> 01:18:18.633
December 29


01:18:25.259 --> 01:18:27.384
Hi.


01:18:30.175 --> 01:18:33.092
-You didn't get any sleep.
-No.


01:18:34.384 --> 01:18:36.467
Tomas!


01:18:39.510 --> 01:18:43.635
We're meeting a researcher
at the Radium Hospital.


01:18:43.760 --> 01:18:48.801
He's only given us 20 min.
Tomas has googled treatments in the US.


01:18:48.926 --> 01:18:53.261
We need to know what
the researcher thinks. Tomas!


01:18:53.386 --> 01:18:56.594
He's so slow it drives me crazy.


01:18:59.636 --> 01:19:04.386
Are you sure this isn't too much for you?
I mean...


01:19:04.511 --> 01:19:09.011
Do you have to get married now?
Just before the operation?


01:19:10.220 --> 01:19:12.970
When should I otherwise do it?


01:19:13.095 --> 01:19:17.679
What do you think? With my wedding
and birthday on the same day,


01:19:17.804 --> 01:19:21.471
you'll only have to remember me
once a year.


01:19:22.804 --> 01:19:25.846
And you'll get fireworks too.


01:19:36.929 --> 01:19:39.013
We have to leave.


01:19:57.931 --> 01:20:00.765
We're fifteen minutes early.


01:20:12.849 --> 01:20:17.642
I have to admit that you're
an interesting case, with complex issues.


01:20:17.767 --> 01:20:22.142
Whether and how to treat someone
with your diagnosis.


01:20:22.267 --> 01:20:26.725
Most lung cancer patients these days
are truck drivers.


01:20:26.850 --> 01:20:30.892
Except for the odd trial lawyer, right?


01:20:31.017 --> 01:20:35.893
Let's sit down over there.
It's too far to go back to my office.


01:20:38.309 --> 01:20:42.768
As I'm sure you already know,
there's no cure in your case.


01:20:43.434 --> 01:20:47.809
All we know for sure is that
you will die from this cancer.


01:20:47.934 --> 01:20:52.894
My advice is not to waste time
searching for miracle cures abroad.


01:20:53.019 --> 01:20:57.894
They don't exist. Or alternative treatment
with no proven effect.


01:20:58.019 --> 01:21:03.061
Or brutal life-extending treatment
that will reduce the quality


01:21:03.186 --> 01:21:05.645
of the life you have left.


01:21:05.770 --> 01:21:09.645
I think all my international
colleagues would agree.


01:21:14.311 --> 01:21:17.478
What would you have done if it were you?


01:21:20.478 --> 01:21:25.312
I guess it's easy to say
when you're not in this situation.


01:21:25.437 --> 01:21:29.730
I don't think I'd put up a fight.
I'd try to enjoy life,


01:21:29.855 --> 01:21:32.772
with wine, good food.


01:21:32.897 --> 01:21:38.563
Be with my family. The children,
the four weeks or so that are left.


01:21:38.688 --> 01:21:45.480
Instead of four months alone in painful
life-extending treatment at a US hospital.


01:21:45.605 --> 01:21:48.563
That's what I'd do.


01:21:55.690 --> 01:21:58.440
That was a pretty clear message.


01:21:58.565 --> 01:22:01.982
No use searching for a miracle cure.


01:22:02.774 --> 01:22:06.899
You didn't have to ask that fool
what he would've done.


01:22:12.607 --> 01:22:18.107
-You wanted to know everything.
-You're not dying. You don't get to ask.


01:22:26.858 --> 01:22:29.026
This one's available.


01:22:31.901 --> 01:22:36.526
We've actually proposed
to each other several times.


01:22:37.526 --> 01:22:42.442
But Tomas was still married
the first time. Then he got separated.


01:22:42.567 --> 01:22:46.776
We wanted to have children.
Then we moved.


01:22:46.901 --> 01:22:49.527
And had more children.


01:22:49.652 --> 01:22:54.735
And work, lots of work.
And sick parents.


01:22:55.818 --> 01:23:00.528
Then there was a time when
we both wanted to get married.


01:23:00.653 --> 01:23:05.819
But Tomas wanted a big wedding,
and I wanted a small one.


01:23:05.944 --> 01:23:12.194
So we never managed to agree. Or rather,
we did set a date many years ago.


01:23:12.319 --> 01:23:15.695
Then Tomas got a job on some project.


01:23:17.404 --> 01:23:20.695
Well, I can't remember.


01:23:20.820 --> 01:23:26.654
There's always been something.
Someone's needs always got in the way.


01:23:26.779 --> 01:23:32.737
Before everything turned sour, and we
no longer knew if we wanted each other.


01:23:32.862 --> 01:23:38.530
But we decided to try a little longer.
That was last Christmas. Then I fell ill.


01:23:38.655 --> 01:23:42.531
Then I recovered, then relapsed.
And here we are.


01:23:51.281 --> 01:23:56.864
-Could we get married in church?
-On New Year's Eve? That won't be easy.


01:23:56.989 --> 01:24:01.697
Because I don't think Anja
wants to get married in a hospital.


01:24:01.822 --> 01:24:04.447
Maybe we could find a chapel?


01:24:04.572 --> 01:24:08.408
We won't be that many.
Maybe thirty people.


01:24:08.533 --> 01:24:13.616
I'll try to pull some strings.
But I can't promise anything.


01:24:13.741 --> 01:24:17.074
I'll get back to you when I know more.


01:24:17.199 --> 01:24:21.324
-I'll call you as soon as I can.
-Thank you.


01:24:31.283 --> 01:24:36.742
How crazy was that? He didn't ask
one single question about who we are.


01:24:36.867 --> 01:24:40.118
Maybe he didn't get the chance.


01:24:42.285 --> 01:24:47.785
He doesn't need to know all the details of
our lives to perform a wedding ceremony.


01:24:47.910 --> 01:24:51.285
-Details?
-Maybe it doesn't matter.


01:24:53.076 --> 01:24:57.326
I think you describe us in a shabby way.


01:24:57.451 --> 01:25:03.577
You paint our life like a complete grind.
That's not how I remember it.


01:25:06.119 --> 01:25:08.827
Then how do you remember it?


01:25:08.952 --> 01:25:13.245
I don't know what you see, Tomas.
Give me some new images.


01:25:15.287 --> 01:25:19.953
-Don't do this to us.
-We haven't lived the same life.


01:25:20.078 --> 01:25:23.495
Life's not... It's not perfect.


01:25:30.579 --> 01:25:36.121
All the times you talked about leaving.
But I never wanted to leave you.


01:25:36.246 --> 01:25:40.079
It's not easy being where you are now.


01:25:40.204 --> 01:25:43.204
But right now you're just ruthless.


01:26:01.831 --> 01:26:05.206
December 30


01:26:05.748 --> 01:26:07.998
-Pancake?
-Yes please.


01:26:10.873 --> 01:26:14.248
-That's your third one.
-No, it's my second.


01:26:14.373 --> 01:26:17.874
-Are you sure?
-I had one, then this one.


01:26:17.999 --> 01:26:20.917
Relax, I'll make some more.


01:26:27.125 --> 01:26:30.833
Vera? Would you be
my maid of honor, with Arthur?


01:26:34.083 --> 01:26:36.292
I'd love to.


01:26:40.917 --> 01:26:44.125
But what do I have to do?


01:26:45.667 --> 01:26:48.626
Walk behind you and hold your veil?


01:26:50.251 --> 01:26:52.335
I wouldn't know.


01:27:00.919 --> 01:27:03.585
But you'll wear a white dress?


01:27:09.127 --> 01:27:10.960
Good.


01:27:28.962 --> 01:27:33.421
This is what it looks like,
the key to the house of God.


01:27:46.755 --> 01:27:49.088
What do you think?


01:27:49.213 --> 01:27:51.630
It's freezing cold in here.


01:27:51.755 --> 01:27:54.088
Too big. Lacks soul.


01:27:56.631 --> 01:27:59.131
It's all that's on offer.


01:28:00.673 --> 01:28:04.173
I'd rather get married outside
in the cemetery.


01:28:06.632 --> 01:28:12.882
It's simpler than it looks on the hanger.
It's beautiful. You have to try it on.


01:28:18.257 --> 01:28:20.924
You can try it.


01:28:24.965 --> 01:28:30.758
There's a mirror here.
You can step up on this box and see.


01:29:08.803 --> 01:29:11.428
Are you feeling sick?


01:29:11.553 --> 01:29:13.636
Yes.


01:29:17.136 --> 01:29:19.969
Maybe you should take a Vival?


01:29:25.054 --> 01:29:27.345
I left them at home.


01:29:44.346 --> 01:29:48.805
-Anja? What are you doing here?
-Hi.


01:29:49.888 --> 01:29:52.222
Hi.


01:29:52.347 --> 01:29:55.889
Hi.
I got your message.


01:29:56.014 --> 01:29:59.764
-I'm all yours tomorrow.
-Are you home already?


01:29:59.889 --> 01:30:04.764
I just have to fetch something.
Tomas is waiting in the car. Hi, Frans.


01:30:06.972 --> 01:30:11.807
I can't even imagine what it's like
to be you right now.


01:30:11.932 --> 01:30:16.515
-Hi, boys. I just have to fetch something.
-Don't peek into my room.


01:30:16.640 --> 01:30:19.058
It's a secret!


01:30:19.183 --> 01:30:23.099
Mom? What are you doing at home?


01:30:23.224 --> 01:30:27.974
I just had to take care of something
before we go to the hospital.


01:30:30.724 --> 01:30:35.891
-Why aren't you out there with the others?
-They're fussing about.


01:30:36.016 --> 01:30:39.516
Like it's a perfectly ordinary wedding.


01:30:45.143 --> 01:30:47.976
But you're my mom.


01:30:48.101 --> 01:30:52.310
I have to run, Julie.
We'll be getting the results.


01:30:52.435 --> 01:30:55.185
Can't I come with you?


01:30:55.310 --> 01:30:57.726
I'm afraid not.


01:31:09.185 --> 01:31:11.311
Hi.


01:31:15.312 --> 01:31:18.020
Anja...


01:31:18.145 --> 01:31:22.645
Your CT scans are clean.
No metastases in your lungs.


01:31:26.853 --> 01:31:29.187
Anja?


01:31:29.312 --> 01:31:32.728
Let's see. I think...


01:31:32.853 --> 01:31:36.562
Take hold of her.
Come over here.


01:31:37.313 --> 01:31:41.938
Take a deep breath. Okay?
Take my hand. Breathe.


01:31:42.063 --> 01:31:46.730
The surgeon was supposed to tell you,
but I just couldn't wait.


01:31:56.730 --> 01:31:58.980
Yes.


01:31:59.105 --> 01:32:01.355
No, no.


01:32:01.480 --> 01:32:05.315
He's older than me,
but I'm the one who's ill.


01:32:07.065 --> 01:32:09.148
We're getting married.


01:32:29.982 --> 01:32:34.483
Hey, I no longer want to know
how much time they think I have left.


01:32:34.608 --> 01:32:38.317
So I'm not going to ask.


01:32:39.108 --> 01:32:43.400
You can sit here.
There's room for you on the bench.


01:32:46.525 --> 01:32:50.817
Sorry I called you at home
during the holidays.


01:32:50.942 --> 01:32:57.110
Don't worry about that. It's not hard
to understand in your situation. Alright.


01:32:57.235 --> 01:33:01.402
I assume you aren't well,
but how is your headache now?


01:33:01.527 --> 01:33:04.652
Is it better or worse than before?


01:33:04.777 --> 01:33:07.194
-It's better.
-Good.


01:33:07.319 --> 01:33:13.527
What I'm going to do now, is explain
what'll happen during the operation.


01:33:13.652 --> 01:33:17.860
So you won't have to speculate.
So you'll both know.


01:33:20.194 --> 01:33:26.112
Here are the MRI images from December 23.


01:33:26.237 --> 01:33:31.071
And this is where
the metastasis is located.


01:33:31.196 --> 01:33:37.237
It's to the right in the image, but it's
in the back of your left hemisphere.


01:33:37.362 --> 01:33:39.362
And... May I touch you?


01:33:39.487 --> 01:33:45.779
We'll enter through a 20 cm incision
in the back of your head,


01:33:45.904 --> 01:33:50.947
up to about here,
to remove the metastasis.


01:33:51.072 --> 01:33:56.113
The grayish, dark area around here,
that's the edema, the fluid.


01:33:56.238 --> 01:34:02.698
It should be substantially smaller now
as a result of the Medrol treatment.


01:34:02.823 --> 01:34:08.864
If the operation is a success, the results
of the CAT scan of your lungs


01:34:08.989 --> 01:34:12.656
might give us a reason
to perform a PET scan


01:34:12.781 --> 01:34:17.407
to see if it's spread to
any other areas in your body.


01:34:18.240 --> 01:34:20.865
But it all depends on the operation.


01:34:21.949 --> 01:34:25.449
May I ask a question?


01:34:25.574 --> 01:34:27.282
Yes.


01:34:27.407 --> 01:34:32.575
What's the risk involved in the surgery
besides the metastasis itself?


01:34:32.700 --> 01:34:37.158
At worst, the operation
may damage the visual cortex


01:34:37.283 --> 01:34:42.491
and your peripheral vision permanently.
You won't be able to drive.


01:34:42.617 --> 01:34:47.367
I don't need to. But I don't want to be
a zombie bride. I must sleep.


01:34:47.492 --> 01:34:53.742
I want to be myself. All I want now
is to sleep one whole night through!


01:34:53.867 --> 01:34:57.367
Can I please get off the Medrol?


01:34:57.492 --> 01:35:04.035
You can't go to zero, but if you halve
the Medrol dose, you'll sleep better.


01:35:05.118 --> 01:35:09.703
-Thank you.
-The reduction may lead to depression.


01:35:09.828 --> 01:35:15.411
So make sure she doesn't start
talking nonsense before the operation.


01:35:15.536 --> 01:35:18.578
-"Nonsense"?
-It probably won't happen.


01:35:18.703 --> 01:35:24.953
But high doses can trigger a psychosis.
Based on what I see and hear now,


01:35:25.078 --> 01:35:29.036
she should halve her dose immediately.


01:35:36.871 --> 01:35:40.246
This was my mom's wedding dress.


01:35:46.330 --> 01:35:48.163
I've kept it.


01:35:51.080 --> 01:35:53.746
Thanks, Vera, but no.


01:35:57.246 --> 01:36:00.996
I want to wear my own dress.
The dark green one.


01:36:02.664 --> 01:36:05.289
It's too somber.


01:36:05.414 --> 01:36:07.872
No.


01:36:07.997 --> 01:36:11.082
It's dark, not black like in a funeral.


01:36:30.499 --> 01:36:33.416
Vera...


01:36:33.541 --> 01:36:35.374
I'm sorry.


01:36:37.416 --> 01:36:41.791
You're not the one who's
supposed to comfort me.


01:36:57.293 --> 01:37:01.043
Did you halve your dose of Medrol?


01:37:04.168 --> 01:37:07.376
-And took a sleeping pill?
-Yes.


01:37:10.001 --> 01:37:13.251
You need to sleep now.


01:37:14.626 --> 01:37:18.419
You need to sleep
for tomorrow to be a good day.


01:37:24.837 --> 01:37:28.170
New Year's Eve


01:37:51.630 --> 01:37:54.797
Hurray, hurray, hurray!


01:37:54.922 --> 01:37:57.880
Happy birthday!


01:38:01.172 --> 01:38:03.172
Happy birthday, Mom.


01:38:06.505 --> 01:38:10.089
What would you like, Anja?
French toast, yoghurt?


01:38:10.214 --> 01:38:12.880
I'm not that hungry, but thanks.


01:38:13.422 --> 01:38:17.298
But you do want
a cup of Vera's fancy coffee?


01:38:17.423 --> 01:38:19.756
Thank you.


01:38:20.506 --> 01:38:22.591
Happy birthday.


01:38:27.216 --> 01:38:31.049
You slept the whole night through.
Like a log.


01:38:31.174 --> 01:38:35.049
-Really?
-You look rested.


01:38:37.924 --> 01:38:41.133
My batteries are dead.


01:38:43.550 --> 01:38:45.550
Anja, I have to leave now.


01:38:45.675 --> 01:38:49.092
Arthur will pick you up here in two hours.


01:38:50.383 --> 01:38:52.508
Where's Mom going?


01:38:53.843 --> 01:38:59.134
-We've got secret plans for Mom.
-I hate secrets.


01:38:59.259 --> 01:39:01.343
I can imagine.


01:39:20.135 --> 01:39:26.344
It won't be a white dress, Julie. I tried
to get one, but it didn't work out.


01:39:28.095 --> 01:39:30.553
It's not that important.


01:39:31.636 --> 01:39:33.720
It's not.


01:39:35.762 --> 01:39:39.179
-Are you disappointed?
-Aren't you?


01:39:39.304 --> 01:39:41.637
No.


01:39:41.762 --> 01:39:44.804
Maybe it's not that kind of wedding.


01:39:45.846 --> 01:39:49.054
I'm not saying it's a shotgun wedding.


01:39:49.179 --> 01:39:51.179
Just...


01:39:57.221 --> 01:40:01.681
-Are you nervous?
-Anja? Phone call.


01:40:06.348 --> 01:40:09.723
-Is it Arthur?
-No, unknown number.


01:40:11.723 --> 01:40:13.806
Hello?


01:40:18.181 --> 01:40:21.723
I don't think we've spoken earlier.


01:40:22.764 --> 01:40:26.514
Maybe you should speak
to Tomas yourself? Tomas!


01:40:27.974 --> 01:40:29.765
I see.


01:40:36.433 --> 01:40:42.058
Thank you, but that's enough. I've already
agreed a date with the operating surgeon.


01:40:44.058 --> 01:40:46.725
This is about my life, not yours.


01:40:53.016 --> 01:40:58.476
Do you have some sort of agreement
with a crazy surgeon called Ulseth?


01:40:58.601 --> 01:41:02.309
He says you agreed
he'd perform the operation.


01:41:02.434 --> 01:41:06.727
We spoke informally via phone
while I was doing research.


01:41:06.852 --> 01:41:12.977
-It was before I knew it was operable.
-He chewed me out for jumping in line.


01:41:13.102 --> 01:41:16.602
Said the timing didn't matter
because there's no hope.


01:41:16.727 --> 01:41:20.311
My god, how can he say that?


01:41:20.436 --> 01:41:25.603
Anja, I haven't agreed anything
with that humiliated surgeon.


01:41:31.686 --> 01:41:33.811
I've got the jitters.


01:41:36.894 --> 01:41:39.770
Vera and I know nothing about weddings.


01:41:39.895 --> 01:41:44.520
-You're the only one with any experience.
-It's been a while.


01:41:47.188 --> 01:41:51.063
I was four years old
the last time Tomas got married.


01:41:53.021 --> 01:41:56.438
-Shall we go?
-Yes.


01:41:56.563 --> 01:42:01.730
Google says the groom shouldn't see
the bride until she comes up the aisle.


01:42:01.855 --> 01:42:04.146
We'll take care of her.


01:42:04.271 --> 01:42:07.355
-You take care of yourself.
-Thanks.


01:42:25.773 --> 01:42:28.982
Have you thought about how you want it?


01:42:32.565 --> 01:42:35.148
You really have wonderful hair.


01:42:37.273 --> 01:42:40.691
Hi.
I finally found something white for you.


01:42:40.816 --> 01:42:44.109
Or rather for Julie.


01:42:44.234 --> 01:42:47.359
The shop wasn't really open. Look!


01:42:47.484 --> 01:42:50.567
-Isn't it beautiful?
-Very. Thanks.


01:42:51.859 --> 01:42:57.609
Tomas is downstairs with Frans, who wants
to say hi. Didn't know he was best man.


01:42:57.734 --> 01:42:59.942
-Are they here now?
-Yes.


01:43:01.900 --> 01:43:06.610
Yes. Tomas...
He wanted a haircut.


01:43:08.068 --> 01:43:14.568
All the other hairdressers are closed,
so I got an appointment for both of you.


01:43:14.693 --> 01:43:18.319
-It's on the house.
-Thank you.


01:43:18.444 --> 01:43:21.277
Hi. How's the bride doing?


01:43:36.695 --> 01:43:38.528
Anja...


01:43:39.528 --> 01:43:46.237
Didn't you hear what Arthur said? You're
supposed to leave me alone until church.


01:43:46.362 --> 01:43:51.571
Can't you see that all this is too late,
this whole ridiculous setup?


01:43:51.696 --> 01:43:55.988
Did it take a death sentence for you
to forget about yourself,


01:43:56.113 --> 01:43:59.780
and suddenly do everything right?


01:43:59.905 --> 01:44:02.697
Now that it's all over anyway?


01:44:04.239 --> 01:44:09.405
How can I walk down the aisle
without thinking it's my own funeral?


01:44:12.780 --> 01:44:17.072
I've been such a coward.
I should've left you ages ago.


01:44:17.197 --> 01:44:19.947
But I've been too exhausted.


01:44:20.072 --> 01:44:25.241
I've been eaten alive
by you and the kids.


01:44:25.782 --> 01:44:30.449
And now I'm stuck here,
feeling like an ungrateful fool.


01:44:30.574 --> 01:44:33.657
Unable to accept anything from you.


01:44:49.574 --> 01:44:51.992
You don't want to?


01:46:35.415 --> 01:46:37.708
Anja...


01:46:37.833 --> 01:46:39.833
Yes.


01:47:55.795 --> 01:48:02.755
Grace be unto you, and peace, from God
our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ.


01:48:03.380 --> 01:48:09.005
Dear Anja and Tomas. You have come here
to enter into matrimony.


01:48:09.130 --> 01:48:12.255
We have gathered to celebrate with...


01:48:56.467 --> 01:49:01.717
...to have and to hold, for better,
for worse, for richer, for poorer,


01:49:01.842 --> 01:49:04.092
until death do you part?


01:49:04.217 --> 01:49:06.300
I do.


01:50:15.472 --> 01:50:19.805
Thank you.
Thank you so much, everyone.


01:50:19.930 --> 01:50:22.014
Shit!


01:50:30.556 --> 01:50:32.640
Hi, Isak.


01:50:51.766 --> 01:50:58.725
About twenty years ago,
I saw two people fall in love.


01:50:59.725 --> 01:51:04.309
Something both those involved denied.


01:51:06.059 --> 01:51:11.768
But I was convinced
they were having an affair.


01:51:11.893 --> 01:51:17.184
Though I was also certain
it would soon blow over.


01:51:17.309 --> 01:51:20.226
I wasn't the only one who thought so.


01:51:25.934 --> 01:51:30.311
Their love seemed impossible.
And I...


01:51:30.436 --> 01:51:33.603
I seem to remember that you, Anja...


01:51:35.270 --> 01:51:39.936
You were furious that
you'd fallen in love with Tomas.


01:51:40.061 --> 01:51:43.103
It didn't suit your plans at all.


01:51:44.061 --> 01:51:49.520
But it's never been more evident
that you're meant for each other.


01:51:55.729 --> 01:51:57.812
No, what the...?


01:51:59.979 --> 01:52:02.062
Darn it. Right.


01:52:02.187 --> 01:52:04.438
Let's take it from the top.


01:52:04.563 --> 01:52:07.647
This is my gift to you.


01:52:10.313 --> 01:52:12.647
You can start it now.


01:52:22.648 --> 01:52:26.981
My ruminations and sad songs are gone


01:52:27.106 --> 01:52:31.356
They never helped me get nothing done


01:52:35.106 --> 01:52:39.107
All the good will and love in the world


01:52:39.232 --> 01:52:43.440
Is what it takes for my little girl


01:52:45.565 --> 01:52:50.316
Should I just cry out? Would it help?


01:52:50.441 --> 01:52:55.191
When I close my eyes, I see myself


01:52:58.441 --> 01:53:02.858
In acrobatic, euphoric high


01:53:02.983 --> 01:53:06.316
Heading to see my


01:53:06.441 --> 01:53:08.483
Cutie pie


01:53:16.443 --> 01:53:20.735
You'll never miss the good old lies


01:53:20.860 --> 01:53:25.235
We're gonna kiss till Jesus cries


01:53:28.735 --> 01:53:32.735
You're afraid that it's too far to go


01:53:32.860 --> 01:53:37.027
How fast I'll run, you'll never know


01:53:39.443 --> 01:53:44.070
If you would give me right of way


01:53:44.195 --> 01:53:48.529
I'd grant you access every day


01:53:48.654 --> 01:53:54.195
And I can smile
Beat up myself


01:53:54.320 --> 01:53:57.654
I've got theatrics


01:53:57.779 --> 01:54:00.612
If nothing else


01:54:01.654 --> 01:54:06.362
When you bring me all of you


01:54:06.487 --> 01:54:09.238
Unbearable, for still


01:54:11.321 --> 01:54:13.780
My heart is split in two


01:54:15.864 --> 01:54:18.364
Romance makes me ill


01:54:32.697 --> 01:54:36.823
-I don't know what to say.
-What about "Happy New Year"?


01:54:37.823 --> 01:54:42.865
I have to say it. I hope for the best.
But I'll be here if I'm needed.


01:54:42.990 --> 01:54:45.907
Ready to take care of the kids.


01:54:55.574 --> 01:55:00.575
I shouldn't have said that.
But I can't stop thinking about it.


01:55:02.242 --> 01:55:06.200
Thank you, Vera,
but the kids have a father.


01:55:43.702 --> 01:55:45.786
Julie?


01:55:57.788 --> 01:56:00.621
I didn't know you existed.


01:56:10.371 --> 01:56:14.454
I wish I could take you with me
in the afterlife.


01:56:16.329 --> 01:56:19.705
New Year's Day


01:56:24.664 --> 01:56:28.290
I'm trying to imagine who you were.


01:56:30.456 --> 01:56:34.790
Why haven't you told us
about any of this before?


01:56:34.915 --> 01:56:38.331
There's so much I didn't know.


01:56:39.331 --> 01:56:43.165
All those secrets before I was born.


01:56:46.832 --> 01:56:49.832
All the grown-ups were so different.


01:56:53.374 --> 01:56:56.624
More direct than I've ever seen before.


01:57:02.750 --> 01:57:04.625
At least you two.


01:57:08.250 --> 01:57:10.333
Different how?


01:57:11.750 --> 01:57:16.126
I didn't know you could be
so loving to each other.


01:57:17.584 --> 01:57:21.793
Like I've never seen before. I mean...


01:57:21.918 --> 01:57:24.834
Maybe once, one summer, ages ago.


01:57:30.751 --> 01:57:33.294
Just like two kids.


01:57:35.002 --> 01:57:38.377
January 2


01:58:19.505 --> 01:58:21.838
Just a moment.


01:58:24.005 --> 01:58:28.338
There. I'm afraid you can't enter
the operating theatre.


01:58:29.422 --> 01:58:32.256
I'll be here when you wake up.


02:04:55.907 --> 02:04:58.490
Subtitles: Erik Grønvold

